\",\n        \"src-append-reply\",\n        \"src-log-term-commit\"\n      ],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"92b25a38705b47deb8c85bbeffd0dda0\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"feedback\": {\n        \"ref_ids\": [\n          \"src-storage-contract\",\n          \"src-send-durability\",\n          \"src-reset-append\",\n          \"src-step-context\",\n          \"src-raw-entry-ready\",\n          \"src-storage-envelope\",\n          \"src-ready-advance\",\n          \"src-leader-admission\",\n          \"src-response-progress\",\n          \"src-candidate-follower\",\n          \"src-append-reply\",\n          \"src-log-term-commit\"\n        ],\n        \"answered\": \"The inspected RawNode entry is explicitly thread-unsafe and sends Propose into raft.Step; a returned proposal call is not an observed commit or application. Followers forward only with a known leader and forwarding enabled; candidates reject proposals; leaders reject proposals during transfer or after losing their own Progress entry. appendEntry assigns current-term sequential indices, appends to the local log, and queues a self MsgAppResp through send. send queues MsgAppResp, MsgVoteResp and MsgPreVoteResp in msgsAfterAppend, including rejections. RawNode's synchronous path exposes remote replies under the Ready persistence contract and retains self replies for Advance. Its asynchronous path places queued replies in MsgStorageAppend.Responses. The Config interface requires reliable per-thread ordering and durable append writes before response delivery; these are caller duties, not effects proved by queue construction. Positive append responses update peer Progress before maybeCommit; the latter asks the tracker for an index and raftLog.maybeCommit additionally requires advancement and a matching nonzero current term. Step handles message terms before dispatch: ordinary lower-term replies exit without reaching the leader consumer; lower-term storage append responses do not stabilize entries but may complete a snapshot. reset discards votes, peer progress and readOnly tracking while retaining the log, and resets own Match to the local last index. Election vote handling checks vote eligibility and log freshness; candidate response handling distinguishes pre-vote from vote responses. These observations connect persistence support (A6) to formation (A1) and message-context filtering (A2), but do not yet establish the full backbone or a violation.\",\n        \"remaining\": [\n          \"Read election production, leader initialization, timer and transfer paths, and the actual tracker/quorum implementations to explain authority acquisition and loss without assuming majority semantics.\",\n          \"Read configuration activation, restart construction, append conflict handling, snapshots, committed-entry application and public completion contracts to close the initial backbone.\",\n          \"Trace pendingReadIndexMessages separately from reset's readOnly replacement before characterizing old pending work across authority transitions.\",\n          \"Inspect the remainder of newStorageAppendRespMsg and its unstable-log consumer before selecting delayed storage completion as a focused discriminator.\"\n        ],\n        \"understanding\": \"updated\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Next recover the missing election/quorum and recovery/application connections and record a partial or usable AuditSpec as warranted. The concrete next discriminator is whether old pending support is invalidated, retained as committed state, or requalified under a new context; the observed term filter and persistence queue are contrary evidence against a generic stale-reply suspicion. No execution or safety conclusion is attributed to these source readings.\",\n        \"question_updates\": {}\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pending_work\": [],\n  \"current\": {\n    \"phase\": \"executed\",\n    \"operation_id\": \"92b25a38705b47deb8c85bbeffd0dda0\",\n    \"action\": \"research\"\n  },\n  \"latest_decision\": {\n    \"operation_id\": \"92b25a38705b47deb8c85bbeffd0dda0\",\n    \"action\": \"research\",\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"selections\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"operation_id\": \"92b25a38705b47deb8c85bbeffd0dda0\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"stop\": {},\n  \"stop_reason\": \"Not started\",\n  \"review_issues\": [],\n  \"run_id\": \"47a26e8525d1425497be35ac5c8a8b23\",\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"51e43aff33654793a0bcec659c0edd69\",\n  \"elapsed_seconds\": 144.92130189900126,\n  \"source_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_13-39-40-etcd_raft-real-run/agent-source\",\n  \"draft_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_13-39-40-etcd_raft-real-run/draft\",\n  \"state_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_13-39-40-etcd_raft-real-run/state.json\",\n  \"product_schemas\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_13-39-40-etcd_raft-real-run/product-schemas.json\",\n  \"submission_schema\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_13-39-40-etcd_raft-real-run/submission.schema.json\",\n  \"method_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_13-39-40-etcd_raft-real-run/audit-method.md\",\n  \"optional_model_method\": null,\n  \"directed_question\": null,\n  \"tools\": {\n    \"agent\": \"codex-cli 0.155.0-alpha.16\",\n    \"implementation\": \"go version go1.26.7 linux/amd64\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"go_module\",\n    \"harness_kind\": \"go_test\",\n    \"harness_filename\": \"assurance_generated_test.go\",\n    \"instructions\": \"Use TestAssurance-prefixed Go tests in the configured package directory; derive its package declaration from actual source. Emit CA_EVENT JSON using fmt.Println or t.Log. Build dependencies are offline. Inspect actua