{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '135,231p' ../agent-source/node.go; sed -n '348,460p' ../agent-source/node.go; sed -n '291,350p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '335,372p' ../agent-source/confchange/confchange.go; sed -n '1,116p' ../agent-source/bootstrap.go; grep -n '\"'^func.*MaybeUpdate'\"\\\\|\"'^func.*MaybeDecrTo'\"' ../agent-source/tracker/progress.go\"","aggregated_output":"\tTick()\n\t// Campaign causes the Node to transition to candidate state and start campaigning to become leader.\n\tCampaign(ctx context.Context) error\n\t// Propose proposes that data be appended to the log. Note that proposals can be lost without\n\t// notice, therefore it is user's job to ensure proposal retries.\n\tPropose(ctx context.Context, data []byte) error\n\t// ProposeConfChange proposes a configuration change. Like any proposal, the\n\t// configuration change may be dropped with or without an error being\n\t// returned. In particular, configuration changes are dropped unless the\n\t// leader has certainty that there is no prior unapplied configuration\n\t// change in its log.\n\t//\n\t// The method accepts either a pb.ConfChange (deprecated) or pb.ConfChangeV2\n\t// message. The latter allows arbitrary configuration changes via joint\n\t// consensus, notably including replacing a voter. Passing a ConfChangeV2\n\t// message is only allowed if all Nodes participating in the cluster run a\n\t// version of this library aware of the V2 API. See pb.ConfChangeV2 for\n\t// usage details and semantics.\n\tProposeConfChange(ctx context.Context, cc pb.ConfChangeI) error\n\n\t// Step advances the state machine using the given message. ctx.Err() will be returned, if any.\n\tStep(ctx context.Context, msg pb.Message) error\n\n\t// Ready returns a channel that returns the current point-in-time state.\n\t// Users of the Node must call Advance after retrieving the state returned by Ready (unless\n\t// async storage writes is enabled, in which case it should never be called).\n\t//\n\t// NOTE: No committed entries from the next Ready may be applied until all committed entries\n\t// and snapshots from the previous one have finished.\n\tReady() <-chan Ready\n\n\t// Advance notifies the Node that the application has saved progress up to the last Ready.\n\t// It prepares the node to return the next available Ready.\n\t//\n\t// The application should generally call Advance after it applies the entries in last Ready.\n\t//\n\t// However, as an optimization, the application may call Advance while it is applying the\n\t// commands. For example. when the last Ready contains a snapshot, the application might take\n\t// a long time to apply the snapshot data. To continue receiving Ready without blocking raft\n\t// progress, it can call Advance before finishing applying the last ready.\n\t//\n\t// NOTE: Advance must not be called when using AsyncStorageWrites. Response messages from the\n\t// local append and apply threads take its place.\n\tAdvance()\n\t// ApplyConfChange applies a config change (previously passed to\n\t// ProposeConfChange) to the node. This must be called whenever a config\n\t// change is observed in Ready.CommittedEntries, except when the app decides\n\t// to reject the configuration change (i.e. treats it as a noop instead), in\n\t// which case it must not be called.\n\t//\n\t// Returns an opaque non-nil ConfState protobuf which must be recorded in\n\t// snapshots.\n\tApplyConfChange(cc pb.ConfChangeI) *pb.ConfState\n\n\t// TransferLeadership attempts to transfer leadership to the given transferee.\n\tTransferLeadership(ctx context.Context, lead, transferee uint64)\n\n\t// ForgetLeader forgets a follower's current leader, changing it to None. It\n\t// remains a leaderless follower in the current term, without campaigning.\n\t//\n\t// This is useful with PreVote+CheckQuorum, where followers will normally not\n\t// grant pre-votes if they've heard from the leader in the past election\n\t// timeout interval. Leaderless followers can grant pre-votes immediately, so\n\t// if a quorum of followers have strong reason to believe the leader is dead\n\t// (for example via a side-channel or external failure detector) and forget it\n\t// then they can elect a new leader immediately, without waiting out the\n\t// election timeout. They will also revert to normal followers if they hear\n\t// from the leader again, or transition to candidates on an election timeout.\n\t//\n\t// For example, consider a three-node cluster where 1 is the leader and 2+3\n\t// have just received a heartbeat from it. If 2 and 3 believe the leader has\n\t// now died (maybe they know that an orchestration system shut down 1's VM),\n\t// we can instruct 2 to forget the leader and 3 to campaign. 2 will then be\n\t// able to grant 3's pre-vote and elect 3 as leader immediately (normally 2\n\t// would reject the vote until an election timeout passes because it has heard\n\t// from the leader recently). However, 3 can not campaign unilaterally, a\n\t// quorum have to agree that the leader is dead, which avoids disrupting the\n\t// leader if individual nodes are wrong about it being dead.\n\t//\n\t// This does nothing with ReadOnlyLeaseBased, since it would allow a new\n\t// leader to be elected without the old leader knowing.\n\tForgetLeader(ctx context.Context) error\n\n\t// ReadIndex request a read state. The read state will be set in the ready.\n\t// Read state has a read index. Once the application advances further than the read\n\t// index, any linearizable read requests issued before the read request can be\n\t// processed safely. The read state will have the same rctx attached.\n\t// Note that request can be lost without notice, therefore it is user's job\n\t// to retry ReadIndex.\n\t//\n\t// Retries must always use new rctxes, and never reuse an rctx already\n\t// passed into ReadIndex. Starting with release-3.7, this restriction is\n\t// lifted, and it is ok to retry the same rctx. Refer to\n\t// https://github.com/etcd-io/raft/issues/392 for more details.\n\tReadIndex(ctx context.Context, rctx []byte) error\n\n\t// Status returns the current status of the raft state machine.\nfunc (n *node) run() {\n\tvar propc chan msgWithResult\n\tvar readyc chan Ready\n\tvar advancec chan struct{}\n\tvar rd Ready\n\n\tr := n.rn.raft\n\n\tlead := None\n\n\tfor {\n\t\tif advancec == nil && n.rn.HasReady() {\n\t\t\t// Populate a Ready. Note that this Ready is not guaranteed to\n\t\t\t// actually be handled. We will arm readyc, but there's no guarantee\n\t\t\t// that we will actually send on it. It's possible that we will\n\t\t\t// service another channel instead, loop around, and then populate\n\t\t\t// the Ready again. We could instead force the previous Ready to be\n\t\t\t// handled first, but it's generally good to emit larger Readys plus\n\t\t\t// it simplifies testing (by emitting less frequently and more\n\t\t\t// predictably).\n\t\t\trd = n.rn.readyWithoutAccept()\n\t\t\treadyc = n.readyc\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif lead != r.lead {\n\t\t\tif r.hasLeader() {\n\t\t\t\tif lead == None {\n\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"raft.node: %x elected leader %x at term %d\", r.id, r.lead, r.Term)\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"raft.node: %x changed leader from %x to %x at term %d\", r.id, lead, r.lead, r.Term)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tpropc = n.propc\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"raft.node: %x lost leader %x at term %d\", r.id, lead, r.Term)\n\t\t\t\tpropc = nil\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tlead = r.lead\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tselect {\n\t\t// TODO: maybe buffer the config propose if there exists one (the way\n\t\t// described in raft dissertation)\n\t\t// Currently it is dropped in Step silently.\n\t\tcase pm := <-propc:\n\t\t\tm := pm.m\n\t\t\tm.From = r.id\n\t\t\terr := r.Step(m)\n\t\t\tif pm.result != nil {\n\t\t\t\tpm.result <- err\n\t\t\t\tclose(pm.result)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\tcase m := <-n.recvc:\n\t\t\tif IsResponseMsg(m.Type) && !IsLocalMsgTarget(m.From) && r.trk.Progress[m.From] == nil {\n\t\t\t\t// Filter out response message from unknown From.\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tr.Step(m)\n\t\tcase cc := <-n.confc:\n\t\t\t_, okBefore := r.trk.Progress[r.id]\n\t\t\tcs := r.applyConfChange(cc)\n\t\t\t// If the node was removed, block incoming proposals. Note that we\n\t\t\t// only do this if the node was in the config before. Nodes may be\n\t\t\t// a member of the group without knowing this (when they're catching\n\t\t\t// up on the log and don't have the latest config) and we don't want\n\t\t\t// to block the proposal channel in that case.\n\t\t\t//\n\t\t\t// NB: propc is reset when the leader changes, which, if we learn\n\t\t\t// about it, sort of implies that we got readded, maybe? This isn't\n\t\t\t// very sound and likely has bugs.\n\t\t\tif _, okAfter := r.trk.Progress[r.id]; okBefore && !okAfter {\n\t\t\t\tvar found bool\n\t\t\t\tfor _, sl := range [][]uint64{cs.Voters, cs.VotersOutgoing} {\n\t\t\t\t\tfor _, id := range sl {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tif id == r.id {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfound = true\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\tif found {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tif !found {\n\t\t\t\t\tpropc = nil\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tselect {\n\t\t\tcase n.confstatec <- cs:\n\t\t\tcase <-n.done:\n\t\t\t}\n\t\tcase <-n.tickc:\n\t\t\tn.rn.Tick()\n\t\tcase readyc <- rd:\n\t\t\tn.rn.acceptReady(rd)\n\t\t\tif !n.rn.asyncStorageWrites {\n\t\t\t\tadvancec = n.advancec\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\trd = Ready{}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treadyc = nil\n\t\tcase <-advancec:\n\t\t\tn.rn.Advance(rd)\n\t\t\trd = Ready{}\n\t\t\tadvancec = nil\n\t\tcase c := <-n.status:\n\t\t\tc <- getStatus(r)\n\t\tcase <-n.stop:\n\t\t\tclose(n.done)\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (c *Config) validate() error {\n\tif c.ID == None {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"cannot use none as id\")\n\t}\n\tif IsLocalMsgTarget(c.ID) {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"cannot use local target as id\")\n\t}\n\n\tif c.HeartbeatTick <= 0 {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"heartbeat tick must be greater than 0\")\n\t}\n\n\tif c.ElectionTick <= c.HeartbeatTick {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"election tick must be greater than heartbeat tick\")\n\t}\n\n\tif c.Storage == nil {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"storage cannot be nil\")\n\t}\n\n\tif c.MaxUncommittedEntriesSize == 0 {\n\t\tc.MaxUncommittedEntriesSize = noLimit\n\t}\n\n\t// default MaxCommittedSizePerReady to MaxSizePerMsg because they were\n\t// previously the same parameter.\n\tif c.MaxCommittedSizePerReady == 0 {\n\t\tc.MaxCommittedSizePerReady = c.MaxSizePerMsg\n\t}\n\n\tif c.MaxInflightMsgs <= 0 {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"max inflight messages must be greater than 0\")\n\t}\n\tif c.MaxInflightBytes == 0 {\n\t\tc.MaxInflightBytes = noLimit\n\t} else if c.MaxInflightBytes < c.MaxSizePerMsg {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"max inflight bytes must be >= max message size\")\n\t}\n\n\tif c.Logger == nil {\n\t\tc.Logger = getLogger()\n\t}\n\n\tif c.ReadOnlyOption == ReadOnlyLeaseBased && !c.CheckQuorum {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"CheckQuorum must be enabled when ReadOnlyOption is ReadOnlyLeaseBased\")\n\t}\n\n\treturn nil\n}\n\ntype raft struct {\n\tid uint64\n\n\tTerm uint64\n\tVote uint64\n\n\treadStates []ReadState\n\n\t// the log\n\traftLog *raftLog\n// the purposes of the Changer) and returns those copies. It returns an error\n// if checkInvariants does.\nfunc (c Changer) checkAndCopy() (tracker.Config, tracker.ProgressMap, error) {\n\tcfg := c.Tracker.Config.Clone()\n\ttrk := tracker.ProgressMap{}\n\n\tfor id, pr := range c.Tracker.Progress {\n\t\t// A shallow copy is enough because we only mutate the Learner field.\n\t\tppr := *pr\n\t\ttrk[id] = &ppr\n\t}\n\treturn checkAndReturn(cfg, trk)\n}\n\n// checkAndReturn calls checkInvariants on the input and returns either the\n// resulting error or the input.\nfunc checkAndReturn(cfg tracker.Config, trk tracker.ProgressMap) (tracker.Config, tracker.ProgressMap, error) {\n\tif err := checkInvariants(cfg, trk); err != nil {\n\t\treturn tracker.Config{}, tracker.ProgressMap{}, err\n\t}\n\treturn cfg, trk, nil\n}\n\n// err returns zero values and an error.\nfunc (c Changer) err(err error) (tracker.Config, tracker.ProgressMap, error) {\n\treturn tracker.Config{}, nil, err\n}\n\n// nilAwareAdd populates a map entry, creating the map if necessary.\nfunc nilAwareAdd(m *map[uint64]struct{}, id uint64) {\n\tif *m == nil {\n\t\t*m = map[uint64]struct{}{}\n\t}\n\t(*m)[id] = struct{}{}\n}\n\n// nilAwareDelete deletes from a map, nil'ing the map itself if it is empty after.\nfunc nilAwareDelete(m *map[uint64]struct{}, id uint64) {\n// Copyright 2015 The etcd Authors\n//\n// Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");\n// you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.\n// You may obtain a copy of the License at\n//\n//     http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n//\n// Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n// distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\n// WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\n// See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\n// limitations under the License.\n\npackage raft\n\nimport (\n\t\"errors\"\n\n\tpb \"go.etcd.io/raft/v3/raftpb\"\n)\n\n// Bootstrap initializes the RawNode for first use by appending configuration\n// changes for the supplied peers. This method returns an error if the Storage\n// is nonempty.\n//\n// It is recommended that instead of calling this method, applications bootstrap\n// their state manually by setting up a Storage that has a first index > 1 and\n// which stores the desired ConfState as its InitialState.\nfunc (rn *RawNode) Bootstrap(peers []Peer) error {\n\tif len(peers) == 0 {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"must provide at least one peer to Bootstrap\")\n\t}\n\tlastIndex, err := rn.raft.raftLog.storage.LastIndex()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\tif lastIndex != 0 {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"can't bootstrap a nonempty Storage\")\n\t}\n\n\t// We've faked out initial entries above, but nothing has been\n\t// persisted. Start with an empty HardState (thus the first Ready will\n\t// emit a HardState update for the app to persist).\n\trn.prevHardSt = emptyState\n\n\t// TODO(tbg): remove StartNode and give the application the right tools to\n\t// bootstrap the initial membership in a cleaner way.\n\trn.raft.becomeFollower(1, None)\n\tents := make([]pb.Entry, len(peers))\n\tfor i, peer := range peers {\n\t\tcc := pb.ConfChange{Type: pb.ConfChangeAddNode, NodeID: peer.ID, Context: peer.Context}\n\t\tdata, err := cc.Marshal()\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tents[i] = pb.Entry{Type: pb.EntryConfChange, Term: 1, Index: uint64(i + 1), Data: data}\n\t}\n\trn.raft.raftLog.append(ents...)\n\n\t// Now apply them, mainly so that the application can call Campaign\n\t// immediately after StartNode in tests. Note that these nodes will\n\t// be added to raft twice: here and when the application's Ready\n\t// loop calls ApplyConfChange. The calls to addNode must come after\n\t// all calls to raftLog.append so progress.next is set after these\n\t// bootstrapping entries (it is an error if we try to append these\n\t// entries since they have already been committed).\n\t// We do not set raftLog.applied so the application will be able\n\t// to observe all conf changes via Ready.CommittedEntries.\n\t//\n\t// TODO(bdarnell): These entries are still unstable; do we need to preserve\n\t// the invariant that committed < unstable?\n\trn.raft.raftLog.committed = uint64(len(ents))\n\tfor _, peer := range peers {\n\t\trn.raft.applyConfChange(pb.ConfChange{NodeID: peer.ID, Type: pb.ConfChangeAddNode}.AsV2())\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n205:func (pr *Progress) MaybeUpdate(n uint64) bool {\n226:func (pr *Progress) MaybeDecrTo(rejected, matchHint uint64) bool {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '205,260p' ../agent-source/tracker/progress.go; sed -n '212,290p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '125,165p' ../agent-source/storage.go; sed -n '180,200p' ../agent-source/storage.go; sed -n '235,310p' ../agent-source/storage.go; sed -n '478,486p' ../agent-source/node.go; sed -n '513,550p' ../agent-source/node.go\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '205,260p' ../agent-source/tracker/progress.go; sed -n '212,290p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '125,165p' ../agent-source/storage.go; sed -n '180,200p' ../agent-source/storage.go; sed -n '235,310p' ../agent-source/storage.go; sed -n '478,486p' ../agent-source/node.go; sed -n '513,550p' ../agent-source/node.go\"","aggregated_output":"\nfunc (ms *MemoryStorage) lastIndex() uint64 {\n\treturn ms.ents[0].Index + uint64(len(ms.ents)) - 1\n}\n\n// FirstIndex implements the Storage interface.\nfunc (ms *MemoryStorage) FirstIndex() (uint64, error) {\n\tms.Lock()\n\tdefer ms.Unlock()\n\tms.callStats.firstIndex++\n\treturn ms.firstIndex(), nil\n}\n\nfunc (ms *MemoryStorage) firstIndex() uint64 {\n\treturn ms.ents[0].Index + 1\n}\n\n// Snapshot implements the Storage interface.\nfunc (ms *MemoryStorage) Snapshot() (pb.Snapshot, error) {\n\tms.Lock()\n\tdefer ms.Unlock()\n\tif i > ms.lastIndex() {\n\t\tgetLogger().Panicf(\"snapshot %d is out of bound lastindex(%d)\", i, ms.lastIndex())\n\t}\n\n\tms.snapshot.Metadata.Index = i\n\tms.snapshot.Metadata.Term = ms.ents[i-offset].Term\n\tif cs != nil {\n\t\tms.snapshot.Metadata.ConfState = *cs\n\t}\n\tms.snapshot.Data = data\n\treturn ms.snapshot, nil\n}\n\n// Compact discards all log entries prior to compactIndex.\n// It is the application's responsibility to not attempt to compact an index\n// greater than raftLog.applied.\nfunc (ms *MemoryStorage) Compact(compactIndex uint64) error {\n\tms.Lock()\n\tdefer ms.Unlock()\n\toffset := ms.ents[0].Index\n\tif compactIndex <= offset {\n\t\treturn ErrCompacted\n\t}\n\tif compactIndex > ms.lastIndex() {\n\t\tgetLogger().Panicf(\"compact %d is out of bound lastindex(%d)\", compactIndex, ms.lastIndex())\n\t}\n\n\ti := compactIndex - offset\n\t// NB: allocate a new slice instead of reusing the old ms.ents. Entries in\n\t// ms.ents are immutable, and can be referenced from outside MemoryStorage\n\t// through slices returned by ms.Entries().\n\tents := make([]pb.Entry, 1, uint64(len(ms.ents))-i)\n\tents[0].Index = ms.ents[i].Index\n\tents[0].Term = ms.ents[i].Term\n\tents = append(ents, ms.ents[i+1:]...)\n\tms.ents = ents\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// Append the new entries to storage.\n// TODO (xiangli): ensure the entries are continuous and\n// entries[0].Index > ms.entries[0].Index\nfunc (ms *MemoryStorage) Append(entries []pb.Entry) error {\n\tif len(entries) == 0 {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\tms.Lock()\n\tdefer ms.Unlock()\n\n\tfirst := ms.firstIndex()\n\tlast := entries[0].Index + uint64(len(entries)) - 1\n\n\t// shortcut if there is no new entry.\n\tif last < first {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\t// truncate compacted entries\n\tif first > entries[0].Index {\n\t\tentries = entries[first-entries[0].Index:]\n\t}\n\n\toffset := entries[0].Index - ms.ents[0].Index\n\tswitch {\n\tcase uint64(len(ms.ents)) > offset:\n\t\t// NB: full slice expression protects ms.ents at index >= offset from\n\t\t// rewrites, as they may still be referenced from outside MemoryStorage.\n\t\tms.ents = append(ms.ents[:offset:offset], entries...)\n\tcase uint64(len(ms.ents)) == offset:\n\t\tms.ents = append(ms.ents, entries...)\n\tdefault:\n\t\tgetLogger().Panicf(\"missing log entry [last: %d, append at: %d]\",\n\t\t\tms.lastIndex(), entries[0].Index)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\nfunc (n *node) Step(ctx context.Context, m pb.Message) error {\n\t// Ignore unexpected local messages receiving over network.\n\tif IsLocalMsg(m.Type) && !IsLocalMsgTarget(m.From) {\n\t\t// TODO: return an error?\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\treturn n.step(ctx, m)\n}\n\nfunc (n *node) stepWithWaitOption(ctx context.Context, m pb.Message, wait bool) error {\n\tif m.Type != pb.MsgProp {\n\t\tselect {\n\t\tcase n.recvc <- m:\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\tcase <-ctx.Done():\n\t\t\treturn ctx.Err()\n\t\tcase <-n.done:\n\t\t\treturn ErrStopped\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tch := n.propc\n\tpm := msgWithResult{m: m}\n\tif wait {\n\t\tpm.result = make(chan error, 1)\n\t}\n\tselect {\n\tcase ch <- pm:\n\t\tif !wait {\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\tcase <-ctx.Done():\n\t\treturn ctx.Err()\n\tcase <-n.done:\n\t\treturn ErrStopped\n\t}\n\tselect {\n\tcase err := <-pm.result:\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\tcase <-ctx.Done():\n\t\treturn ctx.Err()\n\tcase <-n.done:\n\t\treturn ErrStopped\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_map.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=[]\ndef src(i,f,a,b,k='code_observation'):\n sources.append(dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=k));return i\nsrc('src-election','raft.go',850,1084)\nsrc('src-restart','raft.go',437,497)\nsrc('src-replication-send','raft.go',616,711)\nsrc('src-leader-followup','raft.go',1540,1665)\nsrc('src-snapshot-config','raft.go',1835,2040)\nsrc('src-read-release','raft.go',2123,2164)\nsrc('src-read-result','raft.go',2060,2086)\nsrc('src-apply-progress','raft.go',740,774)\nsrc('src-config-options','raft.go',222,340)\nsrc('src-quorum-joint','quorum/joint.go',17,76)\nsrc('src-quorum-majority','quorum/majority.go',116,212)\nsrc('src-tracker-quorum','tracker/tracker.go',157,281)\nsrc('src-peer-progress','tracker/progress.go',205,253)\nsrc('src-log-append','log.go',107,143)\nsrc('src-log-application','log.go',218,273)\nsrc('src-log-pointers','log.go',320,365)\nsrc('src-log-init','log.go',73,98)\nsrc('src-conf-changer','confchange/confchange.go',26,361)\nsrc('src-conf-restore','confchange/restore.go',22,160)\nsrc('src-read-tracking','read_only.go',19,131)\nsrc('src-storage-response','rawnode.go',268,400)\nsrc('src-unstable-stability','log_unstable.go',94,160)\nsrc('src-node-ready-contract','node.go',49,114,'interface_statement')\nsrc('src-node-api-contract','node.go',135,229,'interface_statement')\nsrc('src-node-loop','node.go',348,460)\nsrc('src-guide-storage','doc.go',70,111,'document_statement')\nsrc('src-guide-proposal','doc.go',144,169,'document_statement')\nsrc('src-storage-interface','storage.go',45,124,'interface_statement')\nsrc('src-memory-append','storage.go',247,310)\nsrc('src-bootstrap','bootstrap.go',23,88)\nB=[]\ndef beh(i,a,owner,ctx,trigger,ss,**kw):\n b=dict(id=i,primary_activity=a,execution_owner=owner,protocol_context=ctx,trigger=trigger,source_ids=ss,unknowns=[]);b.update(kw);B.append(b)\nbeh('B-entry','A7','Serialized RawNode caller or node.run goroutine','One local node ID and active leader knowledge','Propose / incoming Step / Ready consumption',['src-raw-entry-ready','src-node-loop','src-node-api-contract'],implementation_guards=['RawNode rejects network local messages and responses from absent peers; Node also filters absent response senders.','Leader admission rejects removed self or transfer in progress; follower may forward; candidate drops.'],external_effects=['Propose return does not certify commitment. Caller observes committed entries and applies them; retries are caller policy.'],async_boundaries=['Node channels serialize core processing; RawNode caller must provide serialization.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Delivers proposals to current role and exposes committed entries to application.'})\nbeh('B-append','A1','raft.stepLeader and raft.appendEntry','Leader term and active Progress map','Admitted MsgProp or initial leader empty entry',['src-leader-admission','src-reset-append','src-election'],implementation_guards=['Own Progress must exist for proposals; no transfer in progress; payload quota; configuration proposals checked against pending applied position unless disabled.'],writes=['Assign term and indices; append unstable log; queue self MsgAppResp.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-local-entry'],async_boundaries=['Self acknowledgment waits in msgsAfterAppend.'],existing_protections=['Commitment does not immediately follow appendEntry.'])\nbeh('B-replicate','A1','raft.maybeSendAppend / handleAppendEntries','Leader/follower logs identified by index and entry term; RPC term','MsgApp production and receipt',['src-replication-send','src-append-reply','src-log-append','src-step-context'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-local-entry'],produces_fact_ids=['F-append-reply'],implementation_guards=['Follower checks previous entry term; conflicts at committed indices panic; follower commit bounded by matching appended prefix.'],important_branches=['Previous index below committed returns committed index without new append.','Conflict rejection carries index/term hint; unavailable leader history uses snapshot.'],external_effects=['MsgApp response enters persistence queue, not direct network delivery.'])\nbeh('B-persist','A6','raft.send plus RawNode Ready/Advance; storage performed by caller','Response batch and local append-thread order','Queued vote/append replies and unstable state',['src-send-durability','src-storage-contract','src-storage-envelope','src-ready-advance','src-node-ready-contract'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-append-reply','F-vote-reply'],produces_fact_ids=['F-persistence-envelope'],durable_effects=['Core emits obligations to caller, not disk writes. Async caller must durably process append before delivering attached responses; sync caller persists before Messages and Advance.'],async_boundaries=['Remote and self responses may arrive after later core transitions.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Self/peer append acknowledgments are published under persistence duties before being used as replication support.','A2':'Vote replies, including self-votes, are held behind persistence before election tally.'},unknowns=['Package doc permits same-batch message send concurrent with entry persistence while Ready.Messages requires after Entries; applicability of that relaxed policy needs separate investigation.'])\nbeh('B-count','A1','raft.stepLeader / maybeCommit / tracker','Leader term and current incoming/outgoing voter sets','Non-rejected MsgAppResp from tracked peer, or configuration switch',['src-response-progress','src-leader-followup','src-reset-append','src-log-term-commit','src-tracker-quorum','src-quorum-joint','src-quorum-majority','src-peer-progress'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-persistence-envelope'],produces_fact_ids=['F-match','F-committed'],implementation_guards=['Step term handling precedes leader consumer; missing peer ignored.','MaybeUpdate only increases Match; quorum evaluates voter IDs, not all tracked learners.','Commit advance requires current term match at quorum index.'],writes=['Update Match/Next and replication mode; advance commit.'],external_effects=['Broadcast new commit; release pending reads after current-term commit.'],important_branches=['Stale rejection indices do not regress Match; valid rejection retries with corrected Next.'])\nbeh('B-vote','A2','raft.Step vote handler','Candidate log identity and requested election term','MsgVote or MsgPreVote',['src-step-context','src-log-term-commit'],produces_fact_ids=['F-vote-reply'],implementation_guards=['Repeat vote, no prior vote/no leader, or future pre-vote; candidate last log is up-to-date.','Lease guard can suppress higher-term requests except forced transfer.'],writes=['Real granted vote records Vote and resets election timer; pre-vote does not record a durable vote.'],external_effects=['Grant or rejection is queued through send.'])\nbeh('B-election','A2','raft.hup/campaign/stepCandidate','Current term, candidacy type and active voter sets','Campaign or election timeout, then vote replies',['src-election','src-candidate-follower','src-tracker-quorum','src-quorum-joint','src-quorum-majority','src-snapshot-config'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-persistence-envelope'],produces_fact_ids=['F-leader'],implementation_guards=['Campaign requires local nonlearner Progress, no pending snapshot, no unapplied committed configuration change.','Pre-vote increments no term; real campaign increments term and records self vote but counts self only via delayed response.','Tally deduplicates sender votes and requires both configured majorities; response type must match candidacy.'],writes=['Won pre-vote starts real campaign; won vote becomes leader, resets progress and appends current-term empty entry.'],important_branches=['Lost election becomes follower; same-term append/heartbeat/snapshot causes candidate to follow.'])\nbeh('B-context','A2','raft.Step/reset/ticks and role transitions','Local term, role and leader identity','Higher/lower-term messages, CheckQuorum, transfer, election changes',['src-step-context','src-reset-append','src-election','src-leader-followup','src-candidate-follower'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-leader'],implementation_guards=['Higher terms usually force follower; pre-vote/lease exceptions explicit.','Lower-term messages normally stop before role handling; stale storage snapshot completion is retained.'],writes=['reset clears peer Match, election tally, readOnly, pendingConfIndex and transfer state; Vote clears only when term changes; own Match initialized to last index.'],important_branches=['Transfer to nonlearner waits for Match at leader last index then sends TimeoutNow; proposal admission stops during transfer; timeout aborts transfer.','CheckQuorum steps down without active voting quorum when enabled.','Committed log and apply progress survive reset; pendingReadIndexMessages also survives, but heartbeat ack tracking does not.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Invalidates old peer replication support and read acknowledgments; does not roll back committed prefix.'})\nbeh('B-config','A4','raft.applyConfChange/switchToConfig and confchange.Changer','Applied configuration with incoming/outgoing voters, learners and staged learners','Caller applies committed configuration change',['src-snapshot-config','src-conf-changer','src-conf-restore','src-node-api-contract','src-config-options'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-committed','F-match'],implementation_guards=['Simple change limits voter set difference to one; joint entry copies outgoing set; exit removes outgoing set and activates staged learners.','Changer validates progress and voter/learner consistency and nonempty incoming voters.'],writes=['Install active Config and copied Progress; retained nodes keep progress; new nodes start Match zero.'],external_effects=['Recompute leader commit under changed quorum; probe new peers; abort transfer to ineligible target; optional leader stepdown on removal.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Changes which Match values qualify for commitment.','A2':'Changes voters used in elections and local eligibility.'},unknowns=['Package guide and API differ on cancellation procedure; accepted change path is clear, cancellation policy needs an entry-specific contract.'])\nbeh('B-recover','A3','newRaft / raft.restore / confchange.Restore','Restart storage state or snapshot index, term and ConfState','NewRawNode / incoming snapshot / lagging follower',['src-restart','src-log-init','src-snapshot-config','src-conf-restore','src-log-term-commit','src-replication-send','src-bootstrap','src-storage-interface'],produces_fact_ids=['F-committed'],implementation_guards=['Restart checks persisted commit within log bounds; starts follower using saved Term/Vote.','Snapshot must advance committed index, recipient must belong to snapshot config and receiver must be follower.'],important_branches=['Matching snapshot index/term fast-forwards commit without replacing log.','Nonmatching accepted snapshot resets unstable history and reconstructs configuration; append response is persistence-gated.','Bootstrap on empty storage creates term-one committed config entries and applies membership before caller persists/applies Ready.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Reconstructs committed prefix and catches followers up; old election/peer progress is not restored.','A2':'Restores membership and saved term/vote; pending snapshot blocks campaigning.'})\nbeh('B-stable','A6','RawNode.newStorageAppendRespMsg / raft.Step / unstable.stableTo','Acknowledgment emission term plus last entry index and entry term','Local append completion response',['src-storage-response','src-step-context','src-unstable-stability'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-persistence-envelope'],implementation_guards=['Response captures raft term separately from entry LogTerm; Step ignores old-term entry stabilization.','stableTo requires extant unstable entry and matching entry term before removing prefix.'],writes=['Advance unstable offset only on accepted identity; snapshot completion also advances applied position.'],important_branches=['New-term HardState-only append carries last unstable identity, allowing later completion to reconfirm prior writes without appending entries again.','Old-term snapshot completion remains valid because committed snapshot state is term-independent.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Protects the log view used for matching and commitment from prematurely relying on storage while conflicting writes remain in progress.','A5':'Async application is limited to stable committed entries.'})\nbeh('B-apply','A5','raftLog.nextCommittedEnts / RawNode acceptReady / raft.appliedTo; external state machine','Committed prefix, applying and applied positions','Ready output / storage apply response / Advance',['src-log-application','src-log-pointers','src-ready-advance','src-storage-response','src-apply-progress','src-node-api-contract'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-committed'],produces_fact_ids=['F-apply-notified'],implementation_guards=['No committed entries issued while snapshot pending; quota limits outstanding apply batches.','Async mode bounds entries by stable offset; sync mode permits unstable entries subject to Ready processing duties.'],writes=['AcceptReady tracks applying; apply response/Advance updates applied and reduces quota; may propose auto-leave joint config.'],durable_effects=['State-machine writes are caller-owned. Async apply completion need not mean durable state-machine write.'],important_branches=['Node Advance API permits advancing while applying, provided successive Ready applications stay ordered; core applied accounting is not independent proof of user-visible application completion.'],cross_activity_effects={'A4':'Application triggers caller configuration activation and automatic joint exit proposal.'})\nbeh('B-read','A1','stepLeader/readOnly/responseToReadIndexReq','Read request context, captured commit index and current leader term','ReadIndex request and contextual heartbeat responses',['src-leader-admission','src-leader-followup','src-read-release','src-read-result','src-read-tracking','src-node-api-contract','src-node-ready-contract','src-config-options'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-leader','F-committed'],produces_fact_ids=['F-read-state'],implementation_guards=['Nonsingleton leader waits for current-term committed entry.','Safe reads collect contextual acknowledgments and require active voting quorum; lease mode relies on CheckQuorum and timing assumptions.'],important_branches=['Singleton bypasses heartbeat quorum path.','readOnly deduplicates contexts and releases queue prefix through acknowledged context.','Requests waiting for current-term commit survive reset and are reissued with current commit and fresh readOnly tracking; previously emitted ReadStates remain request-specific.'],external_effects=['Local ReadState or remote MsgReadIndexResp; caller must correlate request and reach application index before reading.'],unknowns=['Whether version-qualified same-context retry wording permits a context to identify a later invocation requires focused source/version analysis.'])\nF=[]\ndef fact(i,meaning,identity,context,reps,ss,**kw):\n f=dict(id=i,meaning=meaning,identity=identity,validity_context=context,representation=reps,durability='Volatile core state unless explicitly persisted by the embedding caller.',recovery='Reconstructed only as described by the corresponding storage or protocol path.',source_ids=ss,unknowns=[]);f.update(kw);F.append(f)\nfact('F-local-entry','Leader has appended an entry in its in-memory log; no commitment or durable completion follows from this alone.',{'node':'leader ID','entry':'index and entry term'},'Current leader log; uncommitted suffix can be replaced.',['raftLog.unstable.entries'],['src-reset-append'],invalidators=['B-replicate','B-recover'])\nfact('F-append-reply','Receiver formed a MsgAppResp supporting a matching received prefix, or its already committed prefix for an older base. This is a queued assertion, not observed persistence.',{'sender':'response From','term':'RPC term','prefix':'response Index'},'Legal MsgApp producer and follower log matching; subsequent publication has persistence duties.',['msgsAfterAppend MsgAppResp'],['src-append-reply','src-send-durability'])\nfact('F-vote-reply','Node formed a grant or rejection for the requested election phase and term under its local vote/log guards.',{'sender':'voter ID','recipient':'candidate ID','phase':'vote or pre-vote','term':'response Term'},'Real vote and pre-vote are distinct; phase and term select eligible consumption.',['msgsAfterAppend vote response'],['src-step-context','src-election'],invalidators=['B-context'])\nfact('F-persistence-envelope','Core has arranged a response behind the selected persistence interface: an append-thread response envelope, or synchronous Ready/Advance processing. Only a compliant caller turns this arrangement into durable completion.',{'node':'local node ID','batch':'Ready or ordered MsgStorageAppend batch','responses':'captured response identities and terms'},'Sync persistence contract or async ordered durable append contract; response validity is rechecked on receipt.',['MsgStorageAppend.Responses','Ready.Messages','stepsOnAdvance'],['src-storage-envelope','src-ready-advance','src-storage-contract'],durability='Envelope itself is volatile; actual storage effect is external to raft core.')\nfact('F-match','Leader records that the identified peer acknowledged a log prefix through Match in its current tracking context.',{'leader':'local leader ID','peer':'Progress map key','prefix':'Match'},'Subject to Step term filtering and legal peer replies. Membership changes can retain the same Progress but change eligibility.',['Progress.Match'],['src-response-progress','src-peer-progress','src-reset-append','src-conf-changer'],invalidators=['B-context','B-recover'],reinterpreters=['B-config'])\nfact('F-committed','Local raft log regards all entries through committed as decided; establishment is current-term quorum advancement, leader-certified matching prefix, recovered HardState/snapshot, or explicit bootstrap.',{'group':'embedding raft group','prefix':'committed index and matching log history'},'Monotonic local prefix retained through term changes; durable recovery depends on embedding storage contract.',['raftLog.committed','HardState.Commit','Snapshot.Metadata.Index'],['src-log-term-commit','src-log-append','src-log-pointers','src-snapshot-config','src-bootstrap'],durability='Core commit index is volatile until persisted; committed log preservation depends on persisted support and compliant recovery.')\nfact('F-leader','Local node entered StateLeader after its election consumer found a won result over the active voter configuration.',{'node':'local ID','term':'raft.Term'},'Local authority state is not a current network lease or read confirmation.',['state=StateLeader','lead=id'],['src-candidate-follower','src-election','src-tracker-quorum'],invalidators=['B-context','B-config'])\nfact('F-apply-notified','Core has advanced its applied accounting after caller notification; this is not independently observed state-machine or client completion.',{'node':'local ID','prefix':'raftLog.applied'},'Async completion response or synchronous Advance; the Node interface permits overlapping application after Advance under ordered application duties.',['raftLog.applied'],['src-log-pointers','src-ready-advance','src-storage-response','src-node-api-contract'])\nfact('F-read-state','Implementation emitted a request-associated read index via local ReadState or MsgReadIndexResp under its selected read mode.',{'request':'RequestCtx / entry Data','recipient':'requesting node','index':'returned read index'},'Safe-mode quorum, singleton, or lease branch must be distinguished; caller application and correlation duties remain.',['readStates','MsgReadIndexResp'],['src-read-result','src-leader-followup','src-leader-admission','src-node-ready-contract'],durability='Ephemeral notification; not durable decision or completed read.')\n# Follower prefix commitment has its own direct producer edge.\nnext(b for b in B if b['id']=='B-replicate')['produces_fact_ids'].append('F-committed')\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nacts=[]\nfor a in roles:\n bs=[b for b in B if b['primary_activity']==a]\n acts.append(dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=roles[a]['relation'],realization_summary='; '.join(b['execution_owner'] for b in bs),entry_points=[b['trigger'] for b in bs],source_ids=list(dict.fromkeys(x for b in bs for x in b['source_ids']))))\ndef path(s,bs,fs):\n return dict(explanation=s,behavior_ids=bs,fact_ids=fs,source_ids=list(dict.fromkeys(x for b in B if b['id'] in bs for x in b['source_ids'])))\nover=dict(status='usable',rationale='Both principal paths and their persistence, membership, recovery and application connections have been read. Usable means a sourced starting map, not validation of the responsibilities or all variants.',core_gaps=[],open_details=['Resolve synchronous same-batch send wording before using a relaxed caller persistence policy.','Read-only context reuse and version-qualified retry contract need separate investigation.','Storage backend crash behavior and application/client completion implementations are outside this core library boundary; in-repository MemoryStorage is not a disk durability implementation.','Detailed cancellation semantics and alternate API scheduling remain open; accepted membership activation and ordered application paths are mapped.'])\nover['formation']=path('RawNode.Propose or serialized Node loop enters the role-specific state machine. A leader admits entries, assigns term/index and appends locally; a follower forwards only with leader knowledge and enabled forwarding, while a candidate drops. Leader self support is queued, and follower MsgApp validates previous term and reconciles only an uncommitted suffix before queueing its response. send places append/vote responses behind persistence. Async MsgStorageAppend carries responses requiring ordered durable writes; synchronous Ready.Messages and Advance carry corresponding duties. Positive responses increase per-peer Match; configured majority order statistics (minimum of both groups for joint configuration) supply an index, and maybeCommit additionally matches the current term. Commit propagates through append and heartbeat; heartbeat commit is capped by recipient Match. Followers commit matching received prefixes and do not overwrite committed entries. Ready exposes committed entries, with async mode limited to stable local history and all modes pausing entries behind snapshots. The embedding state machine applies them in order, activates config entries, and correlates its own client completion. A successful proposal call has no commitment guarantee.', ['B-entry','B-append','B-replicate','B-persist','B-count','B-apply'],['F-local-entry','F-append-reply','F-persistence-envelope','F-match','F-committed','F-apply-notified'])\nover['context']=path('An election timeout or Campaign starts only for a locally eligible nonlearner without pending snapshot or unapplied committed configuration. Pre-vote leaves term/vote unchanged; real campaign increments term and queues its self vote until persistence. Voters check vote eligibility and last-log ordering; phase-specific replies are tallied once per sender over active voter sets. A won result establishes local leadership, resets replication tracking and appends an empty current-term entry. Higher-term traffic generally steps the node down, with explicit pre-vote and lease exceptions; lower-term traffic is rejected before normal role consumers. CheckQuorum can remove leadership after insufficient recent voter activity. Transfer pauses proposals, catches up an eligible transferee, sends TimeoutNow, and aborts after an election timeout. Membership activation changes voter sets and local promotability; removal stepdown is configurable. Restart rebuilds from storage HardState and ConfState as follower. Snapshot restore accepts a newer committed prefix with recipient membership, either fast-forwarding a matching log or installing snapshot and reconstructed configuration.', ['B-vote','B-election','B-context','B-config','B-recover'],['F-vote-reply','F-persistence-envelope','F-leader','F-committed'])\nover['connection']=path('Authority reset clears tally, peer Match, and heartbeat read acknowledgments but preserves log and committed/application positions; old uncommitted entries can be replaced only above committed. Current-term entry commitment requalifies retained earlier log history. Configuration application changes eligibility of retained Progress, while new members start Match zero and joint votes/commits require both majorities. Queued persistence responses retain original RPC context: stale network replies cannot enter normal consumers, and stale append-thread entry acknowledgments cannot release unstable entries even if entry identities recur. A new-term HardState-only append can reconfirm in-progress history; snapshot and application completions remain term-independent because they concern committed state. Pending reads waiting for the first current-term commit survive reset, then receive a new commit index and new heartbeat acknowledgments in safe mode; already collected readOnly acknowledgments do not survive. ReadState is only a request-specific application-read prerequisite. Committed configuration application also governs campaign eligibility, and automatic joint exit follows applied progress.', ['B-context','B-count','B-config','B-stable','B-apply','B-read','B-recover'],['F-match','F-committed','F-read-state','F-apply-notified'])\nm=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured go.etcd.io/raft core library, Node and RawNode APIs, quorum/configuration/log machinery and Storage interface. Network transport, disk persistence and user state-machine/client completion are caller duties; MemoryStorage is an in-repository in-memory implementation.',protocol_contexts=['Per-instance local ID, term, role, active ConfState and indexed term-tagged log'],external_interfaces=['Node','RawNode','Storage','Ready / Advance','MsgStorageAppend / MsgStorageApply'],ownership=['Node.run serializes core events; RawNode is thread-unsafe and requires caller serialization.'],selection_injection=['Storage, timer schedule, network delivery and application schedule are embedding choices.'],variants=['PreVote','CheckQuorum','ReadOnlySafe / ReadOnlyLeaseBased','AsyncStorageWrites','StepDownOnRemoval','DisableConfChangeValidation'],source_ids=['src-raw-entry-ready','src-node-loop','src-storage-contract','src-config-options','src-storage-interface']),activities=acts,behaviors=B,facts=F,core_overview=over,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='Ready.Messages persistence ordering',disposition='deferred',reason='Package guide allows same-batch entry writes concurrent with message sends; Ready.Messages states after stable append. Preserve conflict for entry-specific caller policy investigation.',source_ids=['src-guide-storage','src-node-ready-contract'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='ReadIndex context retries',disposition='deferred',reason='Version-qualified retry permission and context-keyed pending map need correspondence analysis before an oracle is selected.',source_ids=['src-node-api-contract','src-read-tracking'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='MemoryStorage.Compact',disposition='deferred',reason='Caller must restrict compaction to applied prefix; detailed backend retention/read interplay not mapped.',source_ids=['src-memory-append'],high_consequence=True)])\njson.dump(m,open('core-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nsub=dict(action='research',rationale='Record the sourced two-core-line overview and reusable relationships before selecting a formal question.',sources=sources,map_path='core-map.json',feedback=dict(ref_ids=[s['id'] for s in sources],answered='Recovered election production and active-voter quorum aggregation, configuration activation, restart/snapshot reconstruction, application notifications and two distinct pending-read lifecycles. The map separates queued support from durable completion, local leadership from current read authority, and core applied accounting from user-visible application. Existing term and entry-identity protections explain why stale storage completion is not generically safe to consume. No check has run and no correctness conclusion follows.',remaining=['Select an entry-specific discriminator for the synchronous persistence-order documentation conflict, comparing strict Ready processing against the package guide same-batch policy.','Read-context reuse remains an independent discriminator requiring version/contract applicability.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Next prioritize the persistence-envelope consumer relationship: determine whether the relaxed documented same-batch policy can publish follower support before its entries are durable, or whether a sourced restriction limits the optimization to leader messages. The stricter Ready contract and async durability envelope are concrete counterevidence; source analysis should settle applicability before any claimed violation.'))\njson.dump(sub,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_map.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));p=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(p.stdout);print(p.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
